  "entity_raw": {
    "name_raw": "Putrid Summons",
    "definition_type_raw": null,
    "source_book_raw": "Horror Adventures pg. 91",
    "definition_raw": "Source Horror Adventures pg. 91\nYou summon creatures whose very presence turns the stomach of your foes.\n\nPrerequisites: Spell Focus (conjuration); ability to cast summon monster or summon nature’s ally.\n\nBenefit: When you cast a summon monster or summon nature’s ally spell, you can choose to summon a single creature that exudes a putrid odor or befouls the water surrounding it, granting it the stench universal monster ability. The duration of the sickened condition created by this stench is a number of rounds equal to the spell’slevel. When performing a putrid summon, you summon a creature from the next lower list than the spell you are casting. For instance, if you cast summon monster IV, you summon a creature from the summon monster III list.",
